    "reason": "Remeasured on master f1092a59 after already-merged #449 (resource-right-sizing W1-\u03b1) added the default-off CAESIUM_RESOURCE_STATS_ENABLED paths (runtime resource samplers, OOM evidence, task-run and partition projections), which grew the statement denominators of the packages it touched (internal/atom/docker 385 -> 461, internal/run 7663 -> 7717, internal/job 2302 -> 2322, internal/worker 1757 -> 1776, internal/incident 1821 -> 1827, pkg/env 130 -> 132, internal/atom 0 -> 62) without taking any package below its floor; the unchanged journey reached none of the new paths, so the max-zero diff ratchet refused 18 changed files on master (run 36849067588). The same refresh enables CAESIUM_RESOURCE_STATS_ENABLED=true (100ms sampling) on the journey server, gives it the engine socket through --group-add while keeping UID 10001, and runs the applied fixture once with `caesium run start`, reading the run back over HTTP until it is terminal and through `caesium run partitions --json`; both reads must show a succeeded exit 0 with a sampled, nonzero peak-memory observation. That covers 7 of #449's 18 changed files; the 11 left are the Podman and Kubernetes engines, the remediation-gated incident pipeline and distributed-mode worker/owner code, which this single-node Docker local-mode journey cannot reach. The floors below were measured with that journey on f1092a59's unchanged Go source (two identical local lane runs; integration coverage 8.0 -> 12.7 %). No covered statement was lost and no percentage floor was lowered: 10 existing package floors are raised and 16 packages the journey now covers gain floors. Browser profiles and first-attempt journeys are complete.",
